# Dario Amodei's Predictions About AI Replacing Programming Work

## Executive Summary

Dario Amodei, CEO of <Organization>Anthropic</Organization>, has repeatedly predicted that AI will take over an increasing share of software development work. His predictions evolved from general statements about AI outperforming humans in cognitive tasks (2024) to explicit forecasts that AI would write most or all code (2025) and eventually automate end-to-end software engineering (2026). 【1-e9ccac】【2-0032b5】

---

## Timeline of Predictions

### October 2024 - General Automation of Knowledge Work

In his essay *Machines of Loving Grace*, Dario Amodei argued that powerful AI systems could emerge around 2026 and outperform humans in many cognitive tasks, including software development. While he did not provide a percentage of code generation, he suggested that AI could eventually perform most jobs better than humans. 【1-e9ccac】【2-0032b5】

**Key prediction:**

> Powerful AI could perform most intellectual and knowledge-work tasks, including programming, at a superhuman level. 【1-e9ccac】【2-0032b5】

---

### March 2025 - "90% of Code in 3-6 Months"

At an event hosted by the <Organization>Council on Foreign Relations</Organization>, Dario Amodei made his most widely quoted prediction. 【3-0d28b3】【4-aa992c】【5-7ee6e2】

**Quote:**

> "I think we will be there in three to six months, where AI is writing 90% of the code. And then, in 12 months, we may be in a world where AI is writing essentially all of the code." 【3-0d28b3】【5-7ee6e2】

### Prediction Breakdown

| Timeline | Prediction |
|-----------|------------|
| 3-6 months | AI writes 90% of code |
| 12 months | AI writes essentially all code |

【3-0d28b3】【4-aa992c】

