### January 2026 - Automation of Software Engineering

At the World Economic Forum in Davos, Dario Amodei expanded his prediction beyond coding itself. 【6-77f256】【7-d106e7】【8-6acc6d】

**Quote:**

> AI models could do "most, maybe all" of what software engineers do end-to-end within 6 to 12 months. 【6-77f256】【8-6acc6d】

### Scope Expansion

This forecast was no longer limited to writing source code. It included:

- Requirements analysis
- Code generation
- Testing
- Documentation
- Debugging
- Deployment activities
- General software engineering workflows

【6-77f256】【7-d106e7】

---

### February 2026 - Near-Total SWE Automation

Later, Dario Amodei refined the timeline and distinguished between "writing code" and "performing all software engineering tasks." 【9-f32de3】【10-cce47d】

**Position:**

- 90% of code being AI-generated is a relatively weak metric.
- Full automation should be measured by end-to-end software engineering capability.
- He estimated roughly a 50% chance of complete SWE automation within 1-3 years.
- He considered it extremely likely within 10 years.

【9-f32de3】【10-cce47d】

